==Old English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{w|West Germanic}} ''*mānōþ'', from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*mēnōþs}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|mōnath}} ({{cog|fy|moanne}}), {{cog|osx|mānuth}} ({{cog|nds|Maand}}), {{cog|odt|*mānoþ}} ({{cog|nl|maand}}), {{cog|goh|mānōd}} ({{cog|de|Monat}}), {{cog|non|mánaðr}} ({{cog|sv|månad}}), {{cog|got|𐌼𐌴𐌽𐍉𐌸𐍃}}.

